@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1819 = private unnamed_addr constant [706 x i8] c"## What it does\0ACheck for unrecognized platform names in `sys.platform` checks.\0A\0A**Note**: this rule is only enabled in `.pyi` stub files.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf a `sys.platform` check compares to a platform name outside of a\0Asmall set of known platforms (e.g. \22linux\22, \22win32\22, etc.), it's likely\0Aa typo or a platform name that is not recognized by type checkers.\0A\0AThe list of known platforms is: \22linux\22, \22win32\22, \22cygwin\22, \22darwin\22.\0A\0A## Example\0A```pyi\0Aif sys.platform == \22linus\22: ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```pyi\0Aif sys.platform == \22linux\22: ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Typing documentation: Version and Platform checking](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/spec/directives.html#version-and-platform-checks)\0A", align 1
