@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1827 = private unnamed_addr constant [886 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for Python version comparisons in stubs that compare against patch\0Aversions (e.g., Python 3.8.3) instead of major and minor versions (e.g.,\0APython 3.8).\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AStub files support simple conditionals to test for differences in Python\0Aversions and platforms. However, type checkers only understand a limited\0Asubset of these conditionals. In particular, type checkers don't support\0Apatch versions (e.g., Python 3.8.3), only major and minor versions (e.g.,\0APython 3.8). Therefore, version checks in stubs should only use the major\0Aand minor versions.\0A\0A## Example\0A```pyi\0Aimport sys\0A\0Aif sys.version_info >= (3, 4, 3): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```pyi\0Aimport sys\0A\0Aif sys.version_info >= (3, 4): ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Typing documentation: Version and Platform checking](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/spec/directives.html#version-and-platform-checks)\0A", align 1
