@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1909 = private unnamed_addr constant [700 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `for` loops that can be replaced by a making a copy of a list.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhen creating a copy of an existing list using a for-loop, prefer\0A`list` or `list.copy` instead. Making a direct copy is more readable and\0Amore performant.\0A\0AUsing the below as an example, the `list`-based copy is ~2x faster on\0APython 3.11.\0A\0ANote that, as with all `perflint` rules, this is only intended as a\0Amicro-optimization, and will have a negligible impact on performance in\0Amost cases.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aoriginal = list(range(10000))\0Afiltered = []\0Afor i in original:\0A    filtered.append(i)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aoriginal = list(range(10000))\0Afiltered = list(original)\0A```\0A", align 1
