@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.2037 = private unnamed_addr constant [439 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for declared assignments to the same variable multiple times\0Ain the same assignment.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAssigning a variable multiple times in the same assignment is redundant,\0Aas the final assignment to the variable is what the value will be.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aa, b, a = (1, 2, 3)\0Aprint(a)  # 3\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A# this is assuming you want to assign 3 to `a`\0A_, b, a = (1, 2, 3)\0Aprint(a)  # 3\0A```\0A\0A", align 1
