@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.2048 = private unnamed_addr constant [698 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for methods decorated with `@singledispatch`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `@singledispatch` decorator is intended for use with functions, not methods.\0A\0AInstead, use the `@singledispatchmethod` decorator, or migrate the method to a\0Astandalone function.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Afrom functools import singledispatch\0A\0A\0Aclass Class:\0A    @singledispatch\0A    def method(self, arg): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Afrom functools import singledispatchmethod\0A\0A\0Aclass Class:\0A    @singledispatchmethod\0A    def method(self, arg): ...\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe, as migrating from `@singledispatch` to\0A`@singledispatchmethod` may change the behavior of the code.\0A", align 1
