@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.2093 = private unnamed_addr constant [798 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for any pyproject.toml that does not conform to the schema from the relevant PEPs.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AYour project may contain invalid metadata or configuration without you noticing\0A\0A## Example\0A```toml\0A[project]\0Aname = \22crab\22\0Aversion = \221.0.0\22\0Aauthors = [\22Ferris the Crab <ferris@example.org>\22]\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```toml\0A[project]\0Aname = \22crab\22\0Aversion = \221.0.0\22\0Aauthors = [\0A  { name = \22Ferris the Crab\22, email = \22ferris@example.org\22 }\0A]\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Specification of `[project]` in pyproject.toml](https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/specifications/declaring-project-metadata/)\0A- [Specification of `[build-system]` in pyproject.toml](https://peps.python.org/pep-0518/)\0A- [Draft but implemented license declaration extensions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0639)\0A", align 1
